{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3073504","formula":"C₁₃H₁₂F₃N₅O₅S","hill":"C13H12F3N5O5S","elements":["H","C","N","O","F","S"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"F":3.0,"H":12.0,"N":5.0,"O":5.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Flazasulfuron"},"descriptions":{"en":"Flazasulfuron is a sulfonylurea herbicide used for controlling the unwanted growth of grass, broad-leaved weeds and sedges. The mode of action of flazasulfuron is through the inhibition of the enzyme acetolactate synthase (ALS), which results in the inhibition of amino acid synthesis, cell division and ultimately plant growth. Flazasulfuron can be used on both pre-emergent weeds and post-emergent weeds."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":93539,"mass":407.33,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=CC(=NC(=N1)NC(=O)NS(=O)(=O)C2=C(C=CC=N2)C(F)(F)F)OC","inchikey":"HWATZEJQIXKWQS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-(4,6-dimethoxypyrimidin-2-yl)-3-[[3-(trifluoromethyl)-2-pyridinyl]sulfonyl]urea","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"93539","atoms":39,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.108,"y":0.715,"z":-1.075,"el":"S"},{"x":-6.334,"y":-0.648,"z":-0.27,"el":"F"},{"x":-5.252,"y":0.918,"z":-1.308,"el":"F"},{"x":-4.609,"y":-1.15,"z":-1.494,"el":"F"},{"x":-2.821,"y":1.885,"z":-1.587,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.087,"y":-0.519,"z":-1.865,"el":"O"},{"x":0.445,"y":-0.947,"z":-0.667,"el":"O"},{"x":4.524,"y":-2.835,"z":0.007,"el":"O"},{"x":6.362,"y":1.517,"z":0.401,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.473,"y":1.183,"z":-0.786,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.005,"y":0.496,"z":1.488,"el":"N"},{"x":1.811,"y":0.929,"z":-0.4,"el":"N"},{"x":3.16,"y":-0.971,"z":-0.198,"el":"N"},{"x":4.094,"y":1.241,"z":0.002,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.857,"y":0.338,"z":0.449,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.173,"y":-0.075,"z":0.581,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.646,"y":-0.343,"z":1.861,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.073,"y":-0.233,"z":-0.595,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.8,"y":-0.193,"z":2.954